spec:
  grid: 20-28 rows x 20-28 cols, bg color 4 fills 1-cell border and all gaps
  rectangles: 3-6 dense (no bg inside) rectangles, each with a unique base color (non-bg, non-marker)
  plain_rect: exactly 1 rectangle has only its base color (no marker pixels); size 5-20 x 5-12
  marked_rects: remaining 2-5 rectangles contain base color + one shared marker color
  marker_color: single color shared by all marked rects, distinct from all base colors and bg
  marker_pattern: |
    LR + UD symmetric pattern of marker pixels inside each rect.
    Defined by a set of 1-3 (near_row_edge, near_col_edge) pairs, each >=1.
    For each pair (r,d), marker pixels appear at the 4 corners of the rect at
    row distances r and h-1-r, col distances d and w-1-d.
    Runs that span across center are allowed (left_dist + right_dist <= w-1).
    No marker pixel at exact center row or center col as isolated single pixel.
    Max near_row_edge: 1-2. Max near_col_edge: 1-2.
  rect_sizes: each rect h and w in 5-20; all rects must be large enough to hold the pattern (h >= 2*max_near_row+1, w >= 2*max_near_col+1)
  alignment: exactly 2 marked rects have row-span overlap with the plain rect [observed]
  non_overlapping: 0-3 additional marked rects that do NOT overlap the plain rect's row span
  separation: rects separated by >=1 bg cell; border gap to grid edge = 1
  output: crop of the plain rect filled with base color + marker pattern mapped by edge-relative distances

